      "title": "From John Higgins 15 March 1845",
      "header_text": [
        "From John Higgins 15 March 1845Alford15th March 1845"
      ],
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "text": "I have obtained the offer of another Estate in this Neighbourhood; which I think very likely to suit you; and I enclose a Plan & Particular of it.",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 2,
          "text": "The Estate consists of a small Farm House, but moderate out buildings; (for which a suitable reduction is made in the price) and about 325 Acres of Land of average quality, in the occupation of an industrious good Tenant.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 3,
          "text": "It is situate about 2 Miles from Claythorpe, where your Father has Property; 212 Miles from Alford (my residence) 11 Miles from Louth; and 11 Miles from Spilsby.— The Tithes are commuted at about 4s/3d Pr. acre; parochial charges are very moderate; and the Church has been lately nearly rebuilt; and the Money borrowed has been paid off.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 4,
          "text": "The Price will be about £12’500; and it will yield a steady clear Rental of 314 Pr cent, free from deductions.— Upon the whole, I consider it a good and safe Investment; and I think the price asked does not exceed the value; on the contrary I know a Person who will give that sum if it is declined by you.",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 4"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 5,
          "text": "I am pressed for as early an answer as possible; and",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 5"
        }
      ],
      "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [
        {
          "class": "salute",
          "text": "Dear Sir,"
        }
      ],
      "body_container_count": 1,
      "used_whole_body_fallback": false,
      "editorial_summary": "Summary Reports that he has an offer of an estate of about 325 acres that CD may find suitable.",
      "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1There is a plan of an estate at Beesby, Lincolnshire (see nn. 2 and 3, below) in DAR 210.25. The plan is dated ‘March 1845’. For CD’s intention to invest in farmland and his earlier dealings with Higgins see letter to Susan Darwin, [27 November 1844?].2This location corresponds to that of the farm at Beesby CD subsequently purchased, see n. 3, below.3Robert Waring Darwin paid a deposit of £620 on 7 April 1845 for the purchase of the farm at Beesby (R. W. Darwin’s Investment Book (Down House MS), p. 74). The same amount and date are recorded by CD in his Investment Book (Down House MS).",
      "letter_container_present": true
    },
